20. How do you handle transactions in a Spring Boot application? 
Spring Boot offers support for declarative transactions using @Transactional to manage 
transactions at the method level. 
• Propagation: You can define how a transaction behaves 
with REQUIRES_NEW, REQUIRES_EXISTING, etc. 
• Isolation: Set transaction isolation levels 
like READ_COMMITTED or SERIALIZABLE based on requirements. 
Example: 
@Transactional(isolation = Isolation.READ_COMMITTED) 
public void transferFunds() { 
// Logic for transferring funds 
} 
